  "fields": {
    "responsibility": "Complete fourth request/service/wait/FIFO ownership replacement plus its inseparable VM-global storage and real compiler/consumer prerequisites.35 handwritten paths and51 producer-qualified generated C products; no unrelated staged prototypes or CI changes.",
    "retired": "Repeated waiter capture as request service state; ambiguous physical queue mutation and priority reorder ownership; NaN-dependent iterative owner convergence; fixed VM global-array storage and shared mutable primitive payload; implicit emitted host-layout selection. Preserve public Scheme names, multi-shot continuation, scheduling policy and official build/test entrypoints.",
    "validation": "41 frozen native cases plus6 current frame/replay checks; current21000-cell primitive/root p1/p2 control; complete current startup Make target with6 unknown healthy-VM cases;326 stdlib programs/326 views/740 static units and all original stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools natural exits; original408 cohorts and matched95 review retained;8 compiled builds/16 real composed executions. Original limits/profile unchanged. Exact canonical/generated/artifact equivalence binds publication; no cold whole-build PASS is inferred.",
    "benefits": "Finite least-solution owner propagation handles cycles/NaN without self-supported stale priority, with at most R final key publications. One queue/write authority coordinates service, wakeup and scheduler paths. Shared identity no longer forces fixed per-VM cell capacity; current tools consumer completes. Waiting caller and multiple continuation resumes retain Scheme roots and shared identity. Correctness/bounded-work benefit is distinct from measured runtime speed.",
    "costs": "Scratch grows from2 to R+7 F64 words for the owner plan; graph leases, wait headers, VM pages/lookups and metadata are additional work. Current body medians regress34.51%/29.71% at p1/p2; interpreted median regresses46.64%. These are retained small-sample observations, not universal causal estimates. The value is finite correct owner/queue/root responsibility under cyclic and multi-shot workloads, not proven throughput superiority.",
    "process": "Catalogue responsibility5 of13; one complete result increment3/4 to4/4 only after this whole ASCENT submission succeeds. Independent branch SMP remains1/12,11 families open. Supporting framework/build changes and the four consumer stages do not increment those axes. Cold comparison is a separate user-authorized later build item.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/branch-checklist.org#REQUEST-PRODUCT-CANDIDATE",
    "models": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/models/sysml/request-product.sysml selects the unit,26 predecessor/source/native obligations and five needs. Native SDK/CLI agree on357 fields; ASCENT computes closure and rejects absent/stale evidence. Existing QNT temporal duties and Lean spatial duties remain separate. See submission/source-review.json and source-equivalence.json.",
    "open": "Original fxmul failure and numeric censor remain baseline debt, never PASS. Cold build and whole-workflow peak are unmeasured in the separate user-assigned build item. No independent SMP12 credit, complete CFFI/generational-GC/scheduler redesign, raw owner-death or remote CI admission."
  },
